  "acceptance": [
    {
      "requirement": "Pin Kafka/RFC behavior and independent valid/wrongproof/nonce/escaping/binding/duplicate/malformed proof fixtures.",
      "proof": [
        "48 actual Apache SCRAM server transcripts across SHA256/SHA512, 12 PLAIN decisions, 36 Java parser cases, 12 actual Apache client proof cases, literal RFC7677 vector and 2 exact-AuthMessage extension references per release; 333 executions across 4.1.2/4.2.1/4.3.1.",
        "Rust replays all48 server transcripts+12 PLAIN+literalRFC+2extension references and12 client-first parser fixtures; server-first/final parsing remains Java/client scope.",
        "Actual ASCII-only SCRAM username rejection and UTF8 SCRAM password/PLAIN identity acceptance pinned independently.",
        "Unknown optional extensions are ignored semantically and cryptographically bound to exact raw AuthMessage; deliberately stricter mandatory/duplicate/GS2 binding and terminal failure behavior documented."
      ],
      "artifacts": [
        "oracle/final-matrix/results.json",
        "oracle/final-validation.json",
        "oracle/independent-mechanism-review.json",
        "rust-qa/results.json"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirement": "Persist only salted verifier forms and enforce all requested budgets.",
      "proof": [
        "Credential and CredentialForm contain only Algorithm/Salt/Iterations/StoredKey/ServerKey; derive never automatically stores a password or its other derivatives.",
        "Validated message65536, identity1024, password16384, salt1024, nonce4096, iteration1000000, entries4096, admission256 and worker64 hard ceilings; bounded configurable defaults are documented.",
        "Message parsing has at most16 distinct attributes; imports require salt>=16, iterations>=4096 and exact32/64-byte key sizes.",
        "Identity-count/duplicate/badkey/iteration/nonce/message/password tests and generation rotation/replay cases pass."
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirement": "Tested constant-time crypto API, cryptographic entropy and redacted diagnostics.",
      "proof": [
        "RustCrypto digest0.11.3 CtOutput::Eq invokes ctutils0.4.2 CtEq for exact32/64-byte outputs; both hashes tested equal/first-middle-last mismatches/bothdirections/wronglength, plus actual independent badproof cases.",
        "getrandom0.4.3 fill supplies32-byte generated salts and32-byte nonce suffixes; freshness and length tests pass.",
        "Secret/Credential/CredentialForm/Service/ScramSession/Identity/ScramResult Debug implementations and fixed Error categories redact inputs.",
        "Application buffers use zeroize1.9 alloc; lifetime limitations for library/compiler/caller temporaries explicitly retained."
      ],
      "artifacts": [
        "crypto-api-review.json",
        "rust-qa/results.json"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirement": "Bound expensive work off Tokio and release caller admission on cancellation while in-flight work stays bounded.",
      "proof": [
        "Two failfast semaphore budgets, Tokio spawn_blocking, owned worker permit through actual queued/running completion, cancellation flag before/after job.",
        "Deterministic current-thread test proves different executor/worker ThreadIds, abort releases admission immediately, unfinished worker remains1, new derive returnsBusy, completion permits later success.",
        "A single-thread blocking-pool test proves queued cancelled job never executes after pool unblocks and cannot admit excess workers.",
        "Tokio short try-lock credential access returnsBusy and releases admission under contention."
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirement": "Default graphs unchanged, only approved optional dependencies, no premature SASL wire API claim.",
      "proof": [
        "Locked active Linux graphs exactly match baseline: client60 and broker17 package nodes including features and dependency edges.",
        "Only optional base640.23/hmac0.13/pbkdf20.13/sha20.11/zeroize1.9 added to sasl; default broker feature set remains empty, existing getrandom/Tokio reused.",
        "Stable and Rust1.85 independently pass default, SASL-only and all-feature full-broker suites, strict alltarget Clippy, fmt and strict rustdoc.",
        "SASL mechanism module is not connected to Kafka dispatch/transport/admin; full connection lifecycle, verifiedTLS PLAIN gating, reauthentication and live sessions remain KL11-36."
      ],
      "artifacts": [
        "dependency-graphs/results.json",
        "rust-qa/results.json"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Mechanism/credential foundation only; no Kafka SASL framing, connection lifecycle, reauthentication, live-broker/client interoperability or production qualification claim.",
    "Kafka raw UTF8 passwords are preserved without SASLprep; SCRAM username ASCII restriction matches Apache, PLAIN identities are UTF8. RFC evidence is the pinned vector/AuthMessage subset, not general SASLprep conformance.",
    "PLAIN prefers SHA256 verifier when both are stored, else SHA512; caller-owned credential persistence remains outside the service.",
    "Admitted SCRAM/PLAIN operations retain original immutable credential generations; rotation changes new admissions, not revocation of already admitted exchanges.",
    "Cancelling PBKDF2 cannot preempt its blocking computation; admission drops immediately but queued/running worker and secret remain bounded until actual completion.",
    "CtOutput API/source verification is not statistical timing certification or an all-architecture/compiler guarantee; it does not equalize unknown-user or malformed-message timing.",
    "Zeroizing ownership does not guarantee clearing every PBKDF2 U array, HMAC key-pad/hash temporary, compiler/register/stack copy or caller-made copy.",
    "Default graph equality was actually checked for x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu; no unmeasured target graph claim.",
    "Three expected RFC mutant failures validate the independent oracle; precommit failures and initial2f module-format failure are preserved, no new skipped or ignored tests."
  ],
